<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thomas II Zaremba</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1292">1292</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thomas II Zaremba (d. 1292) was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wroclaw">Wrocław</a> from 1270. He fought a long dispute with Duke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-iv-probus">Henry IV Probus</a> of Silesia over the rights and property of the Church, during which he was besieged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raciborz">Racibórz</a> and the duke was excommunicated. In 1290 the duke reconciled with him and granted the bishops full princely rights in the lands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nysa">Nysa</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/otmuchow">Otmuchów</a>, creating the episcopal duchy.</p></div>
